From cde62e1cf4edb35576177204072138bee92468ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@example.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:26:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): sidebar tells parked kanban work from running
 work [daveey]

A chat whose open cards were only parked (scheduled until tomorrow, blocked on an
operational kind, queued behind an unfinished parent) painted exactly like one
whose worker was running: 26 rows looked busy while 1 card ran.

Backend stamps two subsets of kanban_active on every session row:
- kanban_parked: scheduled, non-human blocked/triage, and todo with an open
  parent (a todo whose parents all finished is about to be promoted: live).
  Replicated remote todo counts as parked (no parent links in the replica; the
  owner promotes ready ones on its next tick). Stamped even when 0 so the
  desktop can tell "none parked" from an older backend.
- kanban_held: local todo whose ancestors include a card blocked on a validated
  human request (the chat waits on a human).
kanban_active itself is unchanged (archive guard and "not done" still see all
open cards). Parked/held come from the same single projection as the counts.

Desktop: kanbanStripeCounts() feeds every sessionStatusStripe caller. Live cards
read as working (no stripe), parked-only as grey "waiting", held as red. Against
a backend without kanban_parked the old behaviour holds.

test_unverified_completion_* expected row dicts gain kanban_parked: 0 (the new
always-stamped field; unverified completions are live, not parked).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
